TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  One port, one supplicant.  The DUT is both the authenticator and the RADIUS server,
  so no second switch and no external server took part.

        tb277  eth4   -- supplicant, tools/eapol.py, MAC 02:0d:b9:00:33:74
             |
             |  EAPOL frames, both directions.  tcpdump on eth4,
             v  filter `ether proto 0x888e`.
    +-----------------------------------------------+
    |  swi_d   AT-x960-56YSQ              <-- DUT   |
    |  port1.0.48: dot1x port-control auto,         |
    |              dot1x control-direction both     |
    |         |                                     |
    |         +--> radius-server local, 127.0.0.1   |
    +-----------------------------------------------+
             ^
             |  console, 115200 baud
        tb277  /dev/u2

  DUT     : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 at 115200 baud, S/N A2WQS700B,
            software sin_x96056-20261019-27.  Not a stack.
  server  : the DUT's own local RADIUS server.  `radius-server local`, NAS 127.0.0.1,
            `radius-server host 127.0.0.1`, `aaa authentication dot1x default group
            radius`.  Users ckmulti1, ckmulti2, ckpeap, cktls.  Methods MAC, EAP-MD5,
            EAP-TLS, EAP-PEAP.  EAP trustpoint `local`.
  link    : tb277 eth4 <-> swi_d port1.0.48 (access port in vlan 48; the DUT's vlan 48
            address is 10.38.22.66/27)
  host    : tb277 eth4 sends EAPOL frames as MAC 02:0d:b9:00:33:74 and captures on the
            same interface
  tools   : tools/eapol.py (supplicant and EAPOL capture) on tb277; tools/tb ckcon for
            the console; tools/qmark.py for the read-only help probe; tools/tb health
            for the two health reads

  Port state before step 1, from `show auth interface port1.0.48`:
  reAuthenticate: disabled, reAuthPeriod: 3600, hostMode single-host,
  CD adminControlledDirections: both, portStatus: Unauthorized, everything else disabled.

